# PLAN-932 native warm-edit admission suite — the file-based independent
# oracle for the admission/refusal classification closure (D-927-2). Every
# check runs the REAL scalar worker through the unified probe runner in the
# explicit `source-v1` observation mode, so each refusal carries its TYPED
# fact on the wire and the parent admits it before judging:
#
#   body-edit.success        V-01/V-04 — a legitimate body-only edit takes
#                             the true single-body fast path (the parent's
#                             per-edit structural admission — unaffected=0,
#                             whole=0, fallback=0, real PE exit — is part of
#                             the green verdict); the judged value is the
#                             independent revision-1 expectation (64).
#   body-edit.language       V-03 — a real type error in the edited body is
#                             a LANGUAGE fact (raw verify/source.type-mismatch),
#                             never washed into a policy refusal or infra.
#   body-edit.repair         V-04 — after a refused (language) edit, the next
#                             legitimate body edit on the same session store
#                             succeeds with the new value (85): a refusal
#                             never poisons the accepted state.
#   sig-edit.refused         V-02 — a true signature edit is REFUSED with the
#                             typed signature-or-context-drift verdict
#                             (PLAN-914 N3: a complete valid typed refusal is
#                             the declared diagnostic completion, stage verify).
#   sig-edit.survives        V-05 — the same session's accepted state still
#                             runs green (the old value 43) after the refusal.
#   multi-decl.invalid       V-03 — an edit interval meeting two declarations
#                             is the typed invalid-edit policy refusal.
#   history.a-b-a            V-04 — edit away and back: the content hit
#                             reuses the historical unit (judged run = the
#                             original value 43).
#
# The FAIL-shape controls (a typed refusal vs a success expectation FAILs;
# an untyped default-mode refusal is an infra ERROR; a bad edit literal is
# an ERROR) and the original 115-function t11 workload legs live in the
# formal host gate (mir_native_incremental_formal_runner_gate); the typed
# fact-admission negatives (missing/unknown kind, contradictions) are
# parent-side unit controls (ac_mn::refusal_tests).

```test-case
case {
  schema: "autolang.case/2"
  id: "ace.m1.nw932.body-edit.success"
  tags: ["ace-m1", "warm-admission", "native-warm-admission-932"]
  links: ["PLAN-932"]
  source: { file: "src/main.at", syntax: "auto", path: "main.at" }
  entry: { mode: "program" }
  checks: [
    { id: "body-edit", adapter: "probe", action: "run",
      options: { recipe: "ac/mir-native-scalar-v1", mn: { entry: "d_main", diagnostics: "source-v1" }, steps: [
        { op: "edit-source", from: "x * 2", to: "x * 3" },
        { op: "run" }
      ] },
      expect: { completion: "success", exit: 64 } },
  ]
}
```

